                <pb facs="0824" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.55/10</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Langhorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-10T11:00:00+00:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>760. Belgian-Dutch frontier temporarily closed. Spanish Minister at The Hague
                    informs me that his courier service with Brussels is stopped for time being, and
                    accordingly it is impossible for this Legation to communicate under seal with
                        Whitlock. It is believed that Spanish
                    courier service will be resumed shortly. Doctor Kellogg of relief commission
                    arrived from Brussels yesterday, having obtained special permission to cross
                    frontier, and states that Whitlock has no
                    diplomatic position, no funds, and no pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langhorne</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
